From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:29:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] KitKat UI P18: navbar IME-rotation suppress, shade
 footer drop, QS gap, opaque scrims

- 18.2 NavigationBarView.orientBackButton: 4.4 never rotated the back
  glyph; suppress the modern IME-visibility rotation in 3-button mode
  (animate back to 0 if set; gestural keeps stock).
- 18.3 FooterViewModel/FooterViewBinder/FooterView: manage/history
  footer button retired (donor shade had none); visibility flow wired,
  re-enable is a one-line flip.
- 18.4 qs_panel_padding_top 80dp -> 48dp (header-height clearance,
  the 80dp reserved the removed modern big-clock header). Partial: gap
  reduced; remainder is QS-fragment clock container margins - layout
  trace pending.
- 18.5 notification_scrim_transparent=true: UNLOCKED-state scrim
  alphas zero (ScrimController mTransparentScrimBackground path) -
  the P3 gradient panel rides the PanelView height animation fully
  opaque, donor 4.4 behavior. Keyguard scrims untouched (state-driven).
---
 packages/SystemUI/res/values/bools.xml        | 10 ++++--
 packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml       |  7 +++-
 .../navigationbar/NavigationBarView.java      | 32 +++++++++----------
 .../footer/ui/view/FooterView.java            | 17 ++++++++++
 .../footer/ui/viewbinder/FooterViewBinder.kt  | 22 +++++++++++--
 .../footer/ui/viewmodel/FooterViewModel.kt    |  6 +++-
 6 files changed, 72 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/bools.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/bools.xml
index 234c6df69d0b..c1de17341144 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/bools.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/bools.xml
@@ -28,8 +28,14 @@
     <!-- Whether to enable clipping on Notification Views -->
     <bool name="notification_enable_clipping">true</bool>
 
-    <!-- Whether to enable transparent background for notification scrims -->
-    <bool name="notification_scrim_transparent">false</bool>
+    <!-- KitKat UI P18.5: the 4.4 shade panel was OPAQUE - it rode the
+         PanelView height animation at full alpha with the grab handle
+         attached; the modern scrim fade (behind/notifications scrims
+         darkening with expansion) reads as a post-4.4 fade. Pinning this
+         true zeroes the UNLOCKED-state scrim alphas (ScrimController
+         mTransparentScrimBackground path), so the P3 gradient panel is
+         fully opaque through the whole open/drag/fling - donor ride. -->
+    <bool name="notification_scrim_transparent">true</bool>
 
     <!-- Control whether to force apps to give up control over the display of system bars at all
      times regardless of System Ui Flags.
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
index acbaf6757aaf..529299b7ead9 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
@@ -721,7 +721,12 @@
     <dimen name="qs_dual_tile_padding_horizontal">6dp</dimen>
     <dimen name="qs_panel_elevation">4dp</dimen>
     <dimen name="qs_panel_padding_bottom">@dimen/footer_actions_height</dimen>
-    <dimen name="qs_panel_padding_top">80dp</dimen>
+    <!-- KitKat UI P18.4: the 4.4 QS panel had the brightness slider
+         immediately under the 48dp header row. The stock 80dp reserved
+         clearance for the modern big-clock header, which P15.1 removed
+         (qs_header_height is 48dp) - that clearance is the dead gap the
+         user saw between header and slider on the expanded shade. -->
+    <dimen name="qs_panel_padding_top">48dp</dimen>
 
     <dimen name="qs_data_usage_text_size">14sp</dimen>
     <dimen name="qs_data_usage_usage_text_size">36sp</dimen>
